well imagine getting hundreds of dollars  in gift cards only to find out they've  already been spent it happened to one  young woman who posted her frustrations  on tick tock well then brian she called  the i-team our david charns got answers  about how this works and what you can do  the next time  you buy a gift card i am so frustrated i  have to share this though because it's  absolutely crazy amanda lindman's  frustration boiling over on tick-tock  all over a gift that's turned into a  headache  him giving me those cards just showed  that he was trying to support  my dream of wanting to open my shop her  boyfriend bought her four  100 dollar apple gift cards at a local  target  but when she went to use them to buy an  ipad the money was gone  to see that all of the money had been  taken we were  like our jaws both dropped she's not  alone a class action lawsuit filed in  federal court over a similar problem  according to court documents a  california woman says she bought a 50  apple gift card for her son at a walmart  but when he went to spend it  the money was gone it is a big  problem like everywhere rhonda mettler  investigates cases like this  with the better business bureau as soon  as a card is activated they've got that  information  and they can just go in and drain it dry  to have access to that number you have  to break a seal so you have to like  slide open the sticker seal it's unclear  right now how the numbers are being  stolen  the cards are activated at the register  and linman says a representative told  her the cards were used within  30 minutes of their purchase okay this  is a huge story time for literally  everyone as she waits for answers  lindman's videos are being watched  thousands of times and the comments are  rolling in  ultimately i just wanted to try to get  the story out and see  who else it was affecting and it's clear  that it's affecting a lot of  people a representative from target  telling the i-team once the card is  activated  only apple can help with a potential  refund apple responded to our inquiry  asking for the customer's information  they have not yet provided a further  response terms and conditions from apple  say neither it nor the store that sells  the card are responsible for quote  any lost or stolen gift cards or use  without your permission  linman says right now she just wants  that ipad in either way  her boyfriend is out 400 bucks someone  else spent  i'm david charns 8 news now david thank  you the better business bureau says  you can protect yourself by checking the  packaging on the card  see if it's been tampered with also  treat the card like cash  and if there's a way to register it do  it we've posted more resources online  at eight newsnow dot com
 

